# ============================================================================
#  gn_ae.py  -  v4.8  (NEW LAST WRITER, runs after gn_ad)
# ============================================================================
#  Fixes the dead JavaScript bridge in the v4.7 WebView UI.
#
#  ROOT CAUSE (v4.7): the bundled page's call() helper unconditionally invoked
#  every bridge method with TWO arguments:
#        n[fn](a==null?'':String(a), b==null?'':String(b))
#  but the OffexBridge @JavascriptInterface methods are declared with 0, 1 or 2
#  parameters (refresh()/copyAddress()/deleteInbox()/openSettings()/openMore()/
#  pickDomain() take none; openMessage/switchTo/deleteSaved/nav/openLink take
#  one; only createInbox takes two).  The Android WebView Java bridge resolves a
#  method by its ARGUMENT COUNT and fails the call when no method matches:
#  "If there is no method with matching number of arguments, the method call
#  fails" (Chromium WebView java-bridge spec).  Because the JS wrapped the call
#  in try{}catch(e){} and the bridge failure is swallowed, every tap on Copy,
#  Refresh, Delete, More, Settings, the nav tabs, a message row, a saved inbox
#  and the domain selector died silently - the page looked perfect but was inert.
#
#  WHAT THIS WRITER DOES
#    1. Rewrites app/src/main/assets/offex_ui.html with the SAME CSS + markup
#       (byte-for-byte identical head/body) and a corrected behaviour layer:
#         * call() forwards exactly the arguments it is given (count == params),
#         * every control is wired with addEventListener (static ids) or a single
#           delegated listener (message rows / saved-inbox rows), so rows created
#           by render() are live too,
#         * a transient spinner on "Create inbox" (resting look unchanged) so the
#           loading state is actually visible (the native spinner lives on the
#           view hidden underneath the WebView),
#         * window.onerror + console.error surface failures instead of swallowing
#           them, and report through the native log() bridge method.
#    2. MainActivity.java: adds a WebChromeClient.onConsoleMessage (routes the
#       page's console/errors to logcat) and a @JavascriptInterface log(String).
#    3. Bumps the version 4.7 -> 4.8 (Config self-version, SupportActivity.VERSION,
#       about_version in all 7 locales).
#
#  Nothing else changes: every bridge method still calls the SAME native method
#  it did before (createInbox keeps MainActivity.this.createInbox() and the
#  rewarded-ad + loading flow), the API endpoints/JSON fields, FCM, the support
#  screen, the bundled notification sounds, the AdMob placements, the
#  notification-permission gate, the multi-language support, the install
#  analytics, the OTP precision fix, the tappable verification links, the
#  circular logo and the remote appearance config are all untouched.
# ============================================================================
